%% title: The failover group's two listeners
%% alt: Clients connect to the failover group's listeners rather than to a server: the read-write listener …-fog names whichever server is primary, and the read-only listener names the readable geo-secondary. appdb on …-sqlp in UK South is replicated to …-sqls in UK West; a manual failover swaps the roles and both listeners follow.
flowchart TB
  c(["sqlcmd, while peered<br/>(names resolve to the<br/>private endpoints)"])
  rw("…-fog.database.windows.net<br/>read-write listener")
  ro("…-fog.secondary<br/>.database.windows.net<br/>read-only listener")
  subgraph fog ["failover group …-fog, Manual: a failover swaps the roles"]
    direction LR
    p("…-sqlp, UK South<br/>appdb, Basic<br/>primary")
    s("…-sqls, UK West<br/>appdb, Basic<br/>geo-secondary,<br/>readable, no writes")
    p == "active<br/>geo-replication" ==> s
  end
  c --> rw
  c -- "ApplicationIntent=ReadOnly" --> ro
  rw -- "names the primary" --> p
  ro -- "names the secondary" --> s
  classDef azure fill:#eaf0fa,stroke:#2563eb,color:#0f1b2d
  classDef client fill:#f4f7fb,stroke:#768498,color:#0f1b2d
  class c client
  class rw,ro,p,s azure
